    "text": "1. Confirm the operation applies only to satellite `SAT-19`; do not alter co-orbital relay `SAT-20`.\n2. Verify:\n   - Clearance `DECOM-7734` is current.\n   - `SAT-19` thruster status is **Armed**.\n   - All payload links indicate `severed`.\n3. Run:\n   `satctl preflight SAT-19 --constellation titan`\n4. Continue only if the output shows:\n   `thrust=nominal orbit=decaying`\n5. **WARNING:** The next step commits `SAT-19` to irreversible atmospheric re-entry. Recovery is impossible after burn ignition.\n6. Initiate the terminal deorbit burn:\n   `satctl deorbit SAT-19 --clearance DECOM-7734 --confirm ignite`\n7. After the burn completes, run:\n   `satctl verify SAT-19`\n8. Confirm the output is:\n   `orbit=terminal beacon=active`",
